{"step_index":117,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T11:29:38Z","input_tokens":12299,"cache_read_tokens":102329,"output_tokens":3808,"thinking":"Constructing the `explainer.py` and `engine.js` files is the next logical step. The `engine.js` file requires integration of four specified architectural improvements, including the completion of Tasks 2.3.\n\n\nMemory addresses are allocated deterministically for both scalar and list container types. Specifically, list containers will be tracked using `WeakMap` to ensure shared references across scopes map to the exact same heap address, avoiding unnecessary copies. The function invocation mechanism should maintain this shared reference property for arguments like lists, preventing unintended data duplication when function calls occur.\n\n\nThe garbage collection task filters unreferenced heap objects, ensuring the Heap UI remains clean during loop iterations when variable references change. The expression evaluator will be modified to support short-circuit evaluation for `or` clauses, stopping evaluation as soon as a truthy clause is encountered within the `evalExpr`, `evaluateCondition`, and `buildExpressionFrames` functions.\n\n\nThe expression evaluator will implement short-circuiting for both 'or' and 'and' clauses. For 'or', if the left clause is true, the right clause will be skipped. For 'and', if the left clause is false, the right clause will be skipped. This behavior ensures that expressions like `i < len(arr) and arr[i] == target` will not cause an index out of bounds error. The short-circuit behavior will be recorded in the expression frames to explain the evaluation process.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\napp_build/explainer.py — Rule-Based Teaching System & Thonny-Style Step Explainer\\n100% deterministic, zero AI APIs. Generates beginner and technical explanations\\nfrom actual runtime execution snapshots, sub-expression frames, and scope/memory models.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List\\n\\nPYTHON_SYMBOL_DICTIONARY = {\\n    \\\"class\\\": \\\"`class` defines a blueprint that groups related functions (methods) together.\\\",\\n    \\\"def\\\": \\\"`def` defines a function or method — a reusable block of code that runs when called.\\\",\\n    \\\"return\\\": \\\"`return` stops the function immediately and sends a result value back to the caller.\\\",\\n    \\\"for\\\": \\\"`for` starts a loop that repeats its indented block once for each item in a sequence.\\\",\\n    \\\"while\\\": \\\"`while` starts a loop that keeps repeating as long as its condition remains `True`.\\\",\\n    \\\"in\\\": \\\"`in` pairs a loop variable with the sequence of values it steps through.\\\",\\n    \\\"range(\\\": \\\"`range(n)` generates a sequence of numbers starting from `0` up to `n - 1`.\\\",\\n    \\\"len(\\\": \\\"`len(x)` counts and returns the total number of items inside list or string `x`.\\\",\\n    \\\"and\\\": \\\"`and` checks if BOTH conditions are True (short-circuits if the left side is False).\\\",\\n    \\\"or\\\": \\\"`or` checks if AT LEAST ONE condition is True (short-circuits if the left side is True).\\\",\\n    \\\"//\\\": \\\"`//` is floor division: it divides and rounds down to the nearest whole integer.\\\",\\n    \\\"+=\\\": \\\"`+=` adds the right-hand value to the variable on the left and stores the new total back in that variable.\\\",\\n    \\\"-=\\\": \\\"`-=` subtracts the right-hand value from the variable on the left and updates it.\\\",\\n    \\\">=\\\": \\\"`>=` tests whether the left value is greater than or equal to the right value (`True` or `False`).\\\",\\n    \\\"<=\\\": \\\"`<=` tests whether the left value is less than or equal to the right value (`True` or `False`).\\\",\\n    \\\"==\\\": \\\"`==` compares two values for equality (`True` if equal, `False` otherwise).\\\",\\n    \\\"!=\\\": \\\"`!=` checks whether\n<truncated 7205 bytes>","Description":"\"Create app_build/explainer.py with Thonny sub-expression, short-circuit, and scope/memory explanations\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CVT\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\code-flow-visualizer\\\\app_build\\\\explainer.py\"","toolAction":"\"Creating app_build/explainer.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Create app_build/explainer.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
