{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T11:30:23Z","input_tokens":3964,"cache_read_tokens":114626,"output_tokens":23381,"thinking":"Planning to create `app_build/engine.js` with a focus on clean code and comprehensive implementation. The primary goal is to include a `MemoryHeapTracker` within the generated engine file.\n\n\nThe memory heap will assign deterministic addresses for data structures like lists and immutable scalars, using a `WeakMap` to track shared addresses. Reference counts will be calculated across stack frames on each step to identify objects for garbage collection, separating live and garbage-collectible objects for the UI. The evaluation of expressions will incorporate a sub-expression stepper, handling nested built-in functions.\n\n\nFocusing on enhancing expression evaluation: ensuring `len` is defined within the appropriate scope to prevent runtime errors like \"len is not defined.\" Implementing strict short-circuiting for logical operators (`and`, `or`) to avoid out-of-bounds errors, explicitly flagging these short-circuiting events for the UI. Generating reduction frames for assignments, control flow, and returns to support a Thonny-style debugging experience, including complete variable scope isolation across call stacks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"// app_build/engine.js — Thonny-Style Python Execution Engine\\n// Zero AI APIs. Includes:\\n// 1. Visual Reference Model (Name -> @Address -> Value Stack & Heap Memory Tracker)\\n// 2. Step-by-Step Sub-Expression Evaluator with Short-Circuit ('and' / 'or') Handling\\n// 3. Global vs. Local Variable Scope Isolation across the call stack\\n// 4. Visual Garbage Collection (Reference counting & unreferenced heap object filtering)\\n\\nconst PRELOADED_PROGRAMS = {\\n  max_subarray: {\\n    title: \\\"1. Maximum Subarray (Kadane's Algorithm — Default)\\\",\\n    defaultInput: \\\"nums = [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]\\\",\\n    algorithmOverview:\\n      \\\"This code finds the largest sum you can get from a continuous section of the list.\\\",\\n    code: `class Solution:\\n    def maxSubArray(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:\\n        c = 0\\n        ans = nums[0]\\n\\n        for i in range(len(nums)):\\n            c += nums[i]\\n\\n            if c >= ans:\\n                ans = c\\n\\n            if c < 0:\\n                c = 0\\n\\n        return ans`\\n  },\\n  binary_search: {\\n    title: \\\"2. Binary Search (Two Pointers: left, right, mid)\\\",\\n    defaultInput: \\\"arr = [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13], target = 7\\\",\\n    algorithmOverview:\\n      \\\"This code searches a sorted list for a target number by checking the middle index (`mid`) and cutting the search range (`left` to `right`) in half.\\\",\\n    code: `def binary_search(arr, target):\\n    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\\n\\n    while left <= right:\\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\\n\\n        if arr[mid] == target:\\n            return mid\\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\\n            left = mid + 1\\n        else:\\n            right = mid - 1\\n\\n    return -1`\\n  },\\n  short_circuit_search: {\\n    title: \\\"3. Short-Circuit Guard: Safe Linear Scan (i < len(arr) and arr[i] == target)\\\",\\n    defaultInput: \\\"arr = [2, 4, 6], target = 9\\\",\\n    algorithmOverview:\\n      \\\"Demonstrates short-circuit evaluation (`and`): when `i` reaches `len(arr)` (3), `i < len(arr)` is False so Python skips `arr[i]` and\n<truncated 77969 bytes>","Description":"\"Create app_build/engine.js with Thonny sub-expression evaluator, short-circuit logic, scope isolation, and Stack/Heap Reference Model with Visual GC\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CVT\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\code-flow-visualizer\\\\app_build\\\\engine.js\"","toolAction":"\"Creating app_build/engine.js\"","toolSummary":"\"Create app_build/engine.js\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
